{
 "date": "2026-11-12",
 "script": "scripts/audit_openalex_profiles.py",
 "rule": [
  "A credit that rests on an OpenAlex author profile (route a: key-log claim minted by openalex_people_works.py; route b: linked credit author-works:openalex-author-orcid) is tested against facts the project already trusts; topic and venue never decide.",
  "Safe whatever else: the work prints the key's ORCID on that authorship, or the key holds the work by independent evidence.",
  "Contradictions: date-before-window (the work is older than the key's career window: birth + 20, else PhD - 10, reviews PhD - 9; career_window.py and the linker's PHD_START); printed name disagrees (link_cited_work_authors.forms / name_level as patched by link_work_people; family differs = no family word in common); an ORCID printed on the authorship that is not the key's; the profile's own ORCID is not the key's (or is another key's); a namesake key holds the same title by independent evidence; date-before-span (a key with no life or PhD years: the work is 50+ years older than the key's earliest independently held work; the linker's span fallback widened, as its 10 years flagged mostly the key's own early works); profile-contaminated (the same profile brings this key two or more date-contradicted works: its other unsupported works for this key are suspect).",
  "Route a: withdraw on date-before-window; hold for review on any other contradiction (date-after-death is not used: in the audit it marked posthumous items and wrong life years, never another person).",
  "Route b: demote to author_candidates on date-before-window, date-before-span, family differs, printed ORCID differs, or when the profile is tied to the key by its ORCID alone (no work of the profile is the key's by independent evidence: indep_works = 0); name-given-differs, title-holder and profile-contaminated credits stay credited and are listed (most name-given hits are initials, nicknames and name-order artefacts of the shared name parser; title holders are mostly duplicate keys; contaminated profiles are about half right)."
 ],
